  "articleBody": "It's easy to overlook your roof until there's a problem, but putting off routine checkups can lead to much bigger issues down the line. Here are some common mistakes homeowners make with their roof maintenance, and how to steer clear of them.\n\nFirst, many folks only do a ground-level visual check. While it's good to keep an eye out, a lot of damage, especially things like lifted shingles or compromised flashing, just isn't visible from the ground. You need a professional to safely get up there and inspect all the nooks and crannies. This leads to our next point: walking on the roof unnecessarily. Unless you're trained and have the right safety gear, walking on your roof can be dangerous for you *and* potentially cause more damage, especially if it's already fragile. Let the pros handle it.\n\nAnother big mistake is ignoring drainage areas. Gutters filled with debris, blocked downspouts, or clogged valleys can cause water to back up and seep under your shingles, leading to leaks and rot. These areas need to be clear for proper water flow. Similarly, neglecting the attic or interior of your home during checks is a miss. Discoloration on ceilings or walls often points to a roof leak that's already progressed. Don't wait for a drip; look for subtle signs.\n\nFinally, many homeowners treat visible debris or minor damage as harmless. A few granules in the gutter, a slightly curled shingle, or a small pile of leaves can all be early warning signs of bigger problems brewing. Promptly addressing repairs identified during an inspection is key to limiting additional damage.\n\nCommon Mistakes to Avoid\nTo truly protect your roof, avoid simply waiting for a major storm to prompt an inspection. Don't assume a new roof is invincible; even new installations benefit from regular checks, especially after a year to ensure everything has settled correctly. A common oversight is also not checking your warranty requirements; some warranties require routine maintenance or inspections to remain valid. Lastly, don't just pick the cheapest option for an inspection. Focus on value, experience, and comprehensive reporting to ensure you're getting a thorough assessment that will actually help you protect your home long-term.\n\nDiscounted Roofing Co. offers honest, reliable services and can guide you through a proper routine checkup. Don't make these common mistakes – let us help you protect your investment. Get in touch for an expert inspection.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}